#import "common.typ": *

#sidebar("Design Notes")[
#strong[Roles.] Bellator (Sōma): Attack and Defend, forcing obstacles, intimidation. Furcifer (Mētis): Feint and Maneuver, infiltration, deception. Savant (Psychē): analysis, investigation, healing. Interlocutor (Pneuma): leads Arguments and Negotiations, contacts. Explorator (Sōma/Mētis): ranged Attacks, ambush, travel and tracking. Adept (Pneuma/Psychē): flexible by Domain. These are role targets, not Effect permissions.

#strong[Writing new abilities and signature items.] Give each one a permission (what it lets you attempt), any specific mechanical effect, a limitation and, for items, a recovery route (§2.1). Use existing Power spends for effects they already cover. An ability that adds a new effect states its timing, cost and limits. Don't write a generic Tychē spend that buys an interrupt, bypasses the script or duplicates a Power spend more cheaply.

#strong[Watch in playtest.] Power-cost discounts used with Effort for Power (Silver Tongue, Analyze, Field Medic, Deadly Precision, Jury-Rig in Generic Focuses). Adept workings: if they overshadow other playbooks, limit Focused Channel to minor and significant workings (Easy and Standard). Don't raise the base working cost to 2: a busy Adept runs out of Pneuma before Resistance is counted. Vehicle signature items are 0 load because they don't come on foot missions; an absent vehicle gives no bonus.
]
